hed registry version so the next read\0arefreshes from it. While a registry is set, its values override\0aset_fee_rate on every registry version change.\00\00\00\00\00\13set_params_registry\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\08registry\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\15get_settlement_window\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\a8Admin hands off control to a new address. Requires the CURRENT admin's\0asignature, not the incoming one \e2\80\94 the new admin doesn't need to do\0aanything to receive control.\00\00\00\0etransfer_admin\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09new_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01{Permissionless alternative to transfer_admin: cross-calls a\0adeployed Multisig and checks is_approved(action_id) instead of\0arequiring the current admin's own signature. Same rationale as\0apause_via_multisig \e2\80\94 arguably even more important here, since a\0asingle lost or compromised admin key otherwise has no recovery\0apath at all for a contract that only ever trusted one signature.\00\00\00\00\1btransfer_admin_via_multisig\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11multisig_contract\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09action_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09new_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01LAdmin-gated contract upgrade: swaps the WASM executable behind this\0acontract's address to whatever `new_wasm_hash` was already uploaded\0avia the Soroban deployer, while keeping the same contract ID and all\0aexisting storage. Storage layout compatibility with the new code is\0athe deployer's responsibility, same as any Soroban upgrade.\00\00\00\07upgrade\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dnew_wasm_hash\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01:Permissionless alternative to `upgrade`, authorized by the\0a**pinned** multisig (`set_upgrade_multisig`) reporting `action_id`\0aexecutable as `Critical`. Swapping the contract's executable is\0athe single most consequential action any of these contracts can\0atake, so the multisig is pinned rather than caller-supplied.\00\00\00\00\00\14upgrade_via_multisig\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09action_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dnew_wasm_hash\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\feEmergency stop: blocks new series creation and new trades\0a(create_series, update_premium, buy_option, write_option). Does NOT\0ablock exercise, set_settlement_price, or reclaim_collateral \e2\80\94 a\0apause should let existing positions wind down, not trap funds.\00\00\00\00\00\05pause\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07unpause\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\11Permissionless alternative to pause(): instead of the single\0aadmin address asserting the pause directly, anyone can trigger it\0aonce a deployed Multisig reports `action_id` as approved \e2\80\94 no\0arequire_auth() needed, since the approval itself (M-of-N signers,\0achecked on-chain by the Multisig) is what's actually authorizing\0athis, not the caller triggering it. Same `action_id`-is-opaque\0acontract as everywhere Multisig is used: it's this caller's job to\0apick a stable id scheme, not Multisig's or options_market's to\0ainterpret one.\00\00\00\00\00\00\12pause_via_multisig\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11multisig_contract\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09action_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\14unpause_via_multisig\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11multisig_contract\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09action_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00vAdmin lists a new option series (strike + expiry + type)\0aPremium is computed off-chain via Black-Scholes and passed in\00\00\00\00\00\0dcreate_series\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aunderlying\00\00\00\00\00\11\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0boption_type\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aOptionType\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cstrike_price\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06expiry\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07premium\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bimplied_vol\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\1fPermissionless alternative to create_series: cross-calls a\0adeployed Multisig and checks is_approved(action_id) instead of\0arequiring the admin's own signature. Same validation and per-\0aunderlying cap apply \e2\80\94 approval changes who can list a series,\0anot what parameters a series may have.\00\00\00\00\1acreate_series_via_multisig\00\00\00\00\00\08\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11multisig_contract\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09action_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aunderlying\00\00\00\00\00\11\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0boption_type\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aOptionType\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cstrike_price\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06expiry\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\07premium\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bimplied_vol\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\005Admin updates premium (e.g. after volatility changes)\00\00\00\00\00\00\0eupdate_premium\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bnew_premium\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fnew_implied_vol\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\cdPermissionless alternative to update_premium: cross-calls a\0adeployed Multisig and checks is_approved(action_id) instead of\0arequiring the admin's own signature. Same rationale as\0acreate_series_via_multisig.\00\00\00\00\00\00\1bupdate_premium_via_multisig\00\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11multisig_contract\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09action_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bnew_premium\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0fnew_implied_vol\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01aAdmin cancels an Active series (e.g. mispriced, or the underlying\0afeed is compromised). Existing position holders then pull their own\0arefund via claim_refund rather than the admin pushing funds to\0aeveryone in one call \e2\80\94 Soroban charges for the resources a call\0atouches, and an unbounded push-refund would scale badly with the\0anumber of open positions.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0dcancel_series\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01IPermissionless alternative to cancel_series: cross-calls a\0adeployed Multisig and checks is_approved(action_id) instead of\0arequiring the admin's own signature. Cancelling a series is\0adisruptive to every open position in it, so gating it behind M-of-N\0aapproval (rather than a single key) is at least as warranted here\0aas for pause.\00\00\00\00\00\00\1acancel_series_via_multisig\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11multisig_contract\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09action_id\00\00\00\00\00\03\ee\00\00\00 \00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\84A position holder in a Cancelled series reclaims what they put in:\0abuyers get their premium back, writers get their collateral back.\00\00\00\0cclaim_refund\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05owner\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bposition_id\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00Moves a Cancelled series' entire remaining refund liability \e2\80\94 every\0anot-yet-claimed position's own premium-net-of-fee or full\0acollateral, tracked incrementally in SeriesEscrow since this\0aseries' first buy_option/write_option \e2\80\94 out of options_market's\0aown undifferentiated token balance and into `vault`, tagged by\0a`series_id`. This is what actually closes the gap documented in\0athe README: today, a writer's collateral refund and a buyer's\0apremium refund both draw from the SAME shared contract balance\0athat every OTHER series' positions draw from too, so nothing stops\0athis series' claims from collectively drawing down funds that were\0anever this series' to begin with. Once quarantined here, vault's\0aown InsufficientEscrowBalance check enforces that claim_refund_-\0afrom_vault against this tag can never pay out more than this\0aseries specifically was ever owed \e2\80\94 a real, provable bound instead\0aof an assumption about the shared pot happening to have enough.\0a\0aPermissionless \e2\80\94 this only relocates the contract's OWN \00\00\00\16escrow_series_to_vault\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0evault_contract\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\84Alternative to claim_refund for a Cancelled series whose refund\0aliability has been moved into `vault` via\0aescrow_series_to_vault: pays this position's own\0arefund out of vault's series_id-tagged escrow instead of\0aoptions_market's own balance. Same eligibility checks and same\0arefund formula as claim_refund \e2\80\94 this only changes WHERE the\0apayout is funded from, not who's entitled to what.\00\00\00\17claim_refund_from_vault\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0evault_contract\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05owner\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bposition_id\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11get_series_escrow\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\99Buy `contracts` options in a series (pay premium in USDC)\0a`contracts` is in PRICE_PRECISION scale (1 contract = 1e7)\0a`max_premium` is slippage protection\00\00\00\00\00\00\0abuy_option\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05buyer\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09contracts\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bmax_premium\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\15Write (sell) options \e2\80\94 lock collateral, receive premium\0aFor calls: collateral = contracts \c3\97 underlying price (covered call)\0aFor puts:  collateral = contracts \c3\97 strike price \c3\97 110% (cash-secured put)\0a`min_premium` is slippage protection: the write fails with\0a`PremiumBelowMinimum` if the net premium the writer would receive\0a(after the protocol fee) is below it, so an `update_premium` cut or a\0a`set_fee_rate` increase ordered ahead of the write can't lock the\0awriter's collateral for less than they agreed to. Pass 0 to opt out.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cwrite_option\00\00\00\05\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06writer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09contracts\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\11collateral_amount\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bmin_premium\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\cbTransfer ownership of an open position from `from` to `to` (issue #51).\0a`from` must sign and own the position. Both parties' `UserPositions`\0alists are updated, and the new owner inherits every right attached to\0athe position (exercise for longs, collateral reclaim and cancellation\0arefunds for either side).\0a\0aShorts are transferable too: their collateral is fully locked in this\0acontract at write time, so the recipient receives only the right to\0areclaim whatever collateral is left after settlement, not an unfunded\0aobligation.\0a\0aFails with `Unauthorized` if `from` isn't the owner, and with\0a`AlreadyExercised` / `AlreadySettled` for a closed position. Blocked\0awhile paused. Transferring to `from` itself is a no-op.\00\00\00\00\11transfer_position\00\00\00\00\00\00\03\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\04from\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02to\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bposition_id\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00uExercise a long position before or at expiry (European = only at expiry)\0aSettlement price must be set by oracle first\00\00\00\00\00\00\08exercise\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05owner\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bposition_id\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\02LSame as exercise(), but for every position_id in one call \e2\80\94 for an\0aowner with several long positions (e.g. bought into the same series\0amore than once) who'd otherwise need one transaction per position to\0awind them all down. All-or-nothing, same as any other Soroban call:\0aif any single position_id in the batch fails exercise()'s own\0achecks (not in the money, already exercised, wrong owner, ...), the\0awhole batch aborts rather than silently skipping it. Capped at\0aMAX_BATCH_SIZE so the batch itself can't be sized to blow through\0athis call's resource budget. Returns the summed payout.\00\00\00\0eexercise_batch\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05owner\00\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cposition_ids\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\d5Permissionless keeper settlement and auto-exercise for in-the-money longs.\0aCan be called by keepers, bots, or any third party after settlement.\0aPayout is unconditionally transferred directly to the position owner.\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bsettle_long\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bposition_id\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00-Oracle sets the settlement price for a series\00\00\00\00\00\00\14set_settlement_price\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05price\00\00\00\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\b3Permissionless alternative to set_settlement_price: instead of a\0atrusted `oracle` address asserting a price, anyone can settle a\0aseries once it's expired by pointing at a live price_oracle\0acontract deployment and letting IT supply the price via a\0across-contract call. No require_auth needed \e2\80\94 the price itself is\0aalready backed by that contract's own feeder-authenticated\0aaggregate, so there's nothing left for a caller to vouch for.\00\00\00\00 set_settlement_price_from_oracle\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0foracle_contract\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\adAdmin pins the price_oracle contract `settle_expiry` reads. Unlike\0a`set_settlement_price_from_oracle`, the batch path never takes an\0aoracle from its (permissionless) caller.\00\00\00\00\00\00\10set_price_oracle\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0foracle_contract\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10get_price_oracle\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\e8\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\aeAdmin adds an existing series to the expiry calendar. Series are\0aindexed automatically by `create_series`; this backfills ones listed\0abefore the calendar existed. Idempotent.\00\00\00\00\00\0fregister_expiry\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\008How many series are listed for `underlying` at `expiry`.\00\00\00\10get_expiry_count\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aunderlying\00\00\00\00\00\11\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06expiry\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\5cSeries ids listed for `underlying` at `expiry`, `[cursor, cursor +\0alimit)` in listing order.\00\00\00\11get_expiry_series\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aunderlying\00\00\00\00\00\11\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06expiry\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06cursor\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05limit\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\e7Permissionless: settles up to `limit` (at most\0a`MAX_EXPIRY_BATCH`) unsettled series listed for `underlying` at\0a`expiry`, starting at `cursor`, against one read of the pinned\0aprice oracle. Settled and cancelled series are skipped, so repeated\0aor overlapping calls are safe. Returns the next cursor; it equals\0a`get_expiry_count` once the calendar is exhausted (a cursor past\0athe end returns it immediately). If the oracle has no fresh\0aaggregate the whole call fails and nothing is settled.\00\00\00\00\0dsettle_expiry\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aunderlying\00\00\00\00\00\11\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06expiry\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06cursor\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\05limit\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\002Writers reclaim unused collateral after settlement\00\00\00\00\00\12reclaim_collateral\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06writer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0bposition_id\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\b7Same as reclaim_collateral(), but for every position_id in one\0acall \e2\80\94 same rationale and same all-or-nothing/MAX_BATCH_SIZE\0acontract as exercise_batch(). Returns the summed reclaim.\00\00\00\00\0dreclaim_batch\00\00\00\00\00\00\02\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06writer\00\00\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cposition_ids\00\00\03\ea\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09get_admin\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\13\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\09is_paused\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cget_fee_rate\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\10get_premium_pool\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\1fget_series_count_for_underlying\00\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aunderlying\00\00\00\00\00\11\00\00\00\01\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00sSeries id listed for this exact (underlying, option_type, strike,\0aexpiry) spec, or `None` if no such series exists.\00\00\00\00\0dget_series_id\00\00\00\00\00\00\04\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0aunderlying\00\00\00\00\00\11\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0boption_type\00\00\00\07\d0\00\00\00\0aOptionType\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\0cstrike_price\00\00\00\0b\00\00\00\00\00\00\00\06expiry\00\00\00\00\00\06\00\00\00\01\0